.\" Contact michal.h21@gmail.com to correct errors or typos.
.TH CTANBIB 1 "{{date}}" "{{version}}" "ctanbib man page"
.SH NAME
ctanbib - convert CTAN package information to BibTeX format
.SH SYNOPSIS
ctanbib [\fIoptions\fP] \fIpackage-name\fP ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
This command looks up the Catalogue entry for each \fIpackage-name\fP on CTAN (at
https://ctan.org/xml/2.0/pkg/\fIpackage-name\fP), and converts relevant
information to a BibTeX entry.
.PP
By default, the \fIurl\fP field in the output entry is the package's \fIhome\fP
field value if that is specified in the Catalogue entry; if it isn't,
https://ctan.org/pkg/\fIpackage-name\fP is used.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-ctan\fP
Always use the CTAN \fI/pkg/\fP URL instead of the package homepage.
.TP
\fB\-C, \-\-ctanpath\fP
Use the package's CTAN path as the \fIurl\fP (e.g., \fI/support/ctanbib\fP).
.TP
\fB\-e, \-\-entrytype\fP \fItype\fP
Change the BibTeX entry type. The default is \fImanual\fP.
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fP
Print the help message.
.TP
\fB\-l, \-\-labelformat\fP \fIformat\fP
Change the label format. The default is \fIpkgname\fP. See \fBLabel formats\fP.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output\fP \fIfile\fP
Write output to \fIfile\fP instead of standard output. The default is empty,
i.e. write to standard output.
.TP
\fB\-p, \-\-pkgname\fP
Wrap the package name in a \fB\\ctanbibpkgname\fP command.
This command can be redefined in the document for the desired formatting.
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-separator\fP \fIseparator\fP
Change the label separator. The default is a colon (\fI:\fP).
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-version\fP
Print version information.

.SH LABEL FORMATS
The following formats are available for \fB\-l, \-\-labelformat\fP:
.TP
\fIpkgname\fP
Use the package name as the label.
.TP
\fIpkgname-version\fP
Use the package name and version as the label. If the version is not
available, use the package date instead.
.TP
\fIpkgname-date\fP
Use the package name and date as the label.
.TP
\fIpkgname-date-version\fP
Use the package name, date, and version as the label.
.TP
\fIpkgname-year\fP
Use the package name and the year extracted from its date as the label.
.TP
\fIauthor-year\fP
Use the package author and the year extracted from its date as the label.
If the author is not available, use the package name instead.

.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
ctanbib latex
.EE
.PP
This minimal invocation will print data using conventional BibTeX fields to standard output:
.EX

@manual{latex,
  title = {The LaTeX package},
  subtitle = {A TeX macro package that defines LaTeX},
  author = {Lamport, Leslie and {The LaTeX Project Team}},
  url = {https://www.latex-project.org/},
  urldate = {2026-11-09},
  date = {2026-11-01},
  version = {},
}
.EE
.PP
Note that the output does not use TeX control sequences or have
completely correct capitalization. \fBctanbib\fP works only from the
(plain text) data available from CTAN; any typesetting niceties are up
to you.

.PP
With the \fB\-\-entrytype\fP option:
.EX
ctanbib -e ctan hyperref
.EE
.PP
This produces a bib record with the @ctan type:
.EX

@ctan{hyperref,
  title = {The hyperref package},
  subtitle = {Extensive support for hypertext in LaTeX},
  author = {Oberdiek, Heiko 
     and Rahtz, Sebastian 
     and {The LaTeX Project Team}},
  url = {https://github.com/latex3/hyperref},
  urldate = {2026-11-09},
  date = {2026-11-03},
  version = {7.01t},
}
.EE
.PP
To write the result to a file:
.EX
ctanbib -o ctanbib.bib latex hyperref
.EE
.PP
To use a custom label format and separator:
.EX
ctanbib -l author-year -s "-" latex
.EE

.SH SEE ALSO
See ctanbib-doc.pdf (run: texdoc ctanbib) for more details.
.PP
